1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,050
Every day, people report suspicious links, and platforms have to decide whether a link is safe to publish.

2
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:07,895
Checking each one by hand is slow.

3
00:00:07,895 --> 00:00:13,428
This sample triages a link in about twenty seconds, with the evidence a person needs to make the call.

4
00:00:14,228 --> 00:00:16,117
It runs in your own AWS account.

5
00:00:16,117 --> 00:00:27,215
When you submit a URL, three specialist agents on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore start at the same time: one checks the link and its domain, one looks at the page, and one reads the page's code.

6
00:00:27,215 --> 00:00:32,765
The page opens in AgentCore Browser, an isolated browser that AWS runs, never on your machine.

7
00:00:32,765 --> 00:00:36,956
An orchestrator agent then weighs their findings and gives the verdict.

8
00:00:37,756 --> 00:00:39,539
Let's scan a well-known page.

9
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:45,442
The app shows each agent's progress, and the verdict arrives first: legitimate, low risk, allow.

10
00:00:45,442 --> 00:00:48,148
The full report follows a few seconds later.

11
00:00:53,148 --> 00:00:55,696
Here is a link from a public phishing feed.

12
00:00:55,696 --> 00:00:57,829
Verdict: phishing, high risk, block.

13
00:00:57,829 --> 00:01:07,370
All three specialists agree: a look-alike of a gaming site's domain, a copied profile page, and sign-in buttons that load a cloned login page from the same host.

14
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:13,592
The screenshot was taken in the isolated browser, and the report explains the decision in plain language.

15
00:01:13,592 --> 00:01:17,148
Every verdict is advisory, so a person makes the final call.

16
00:01:21,038 --> 00:01:26,950
You can upload a CSV of up to two hundred URLs in the app, or up to a thousand through the API.

17
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:30,124
Each URL gets its own verdict, risk, time and cost.

18
00:01:30,124 --> 00:01:35,414
Dead links and pages that answer 404 get a fixed answer without an orchestrator call.

19
00:01:37,578 --> 00:01:39,450
The same API powers the app.

20
00:01:39,450 --> 00:01:41,857
Every call is signed with AWS SigV4.

21
00:01:41,857 --> 00:01:47,874
A publish flow can submit a URL, wait for the verdict, and hold anything risky for review.

22
00:01:48,674 --> 00:01:51,870
We measured the default on four hundred and seven live URLs.

23
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:57,196
It caught eighty eight percent of the phishing links, with a false positive rate under five percent.

24
00:01:57,196 --> 00:02:05,186
The median scan took under nineteen seconds, at nine cents of model cost per scan, about half the time and a third less cost than the previous design.

25
00:02:05,986 --> 00:02:08,793
One command deploys it, and one command removes it.

26
00:02:08,793 --> 00:02:13,858
Clone the repository, follow the getting started guide, and scan your first link in minutes.
